## WAKE Phase — Research Direction Finding

**TEST-04a is a mechanism-class failure (sign reversed), not a magnitude miss.**

The distinction matters for the research program:
- A *magnitude miss* (predicted 0.418, observed 0.45) can be repaired by retuning.
- A *mechanism-class failure* (predicted suppression below ΛCDM, observed enhancement above ΛCDM) cannot be repaired within the same mechanism class. Any G_local/G_global suppressor predicts fσ₈ below ΛCDM at all z. DESI DR1 observes fσ₈ above ΛCDM at LRG1, LRG2, combined sigma_8.

Branch 1 diagnosis (sign error in the C_cosmic/C_galactic ratio assignment): since C(rho) is monotonically increasing and galactic halo densities are ~60× higher than the cosmic background, C_galactic > C_cosmic. If G_local/G_global = C_galactic/C_cosmic (instead of C_cosmic/C_galactic), the mechanism predicts enhancement — matching DESI DR1 direction.

Research proposal filed: Synchronism/Research/proposals/test04a_mechanism_class_sign_failure.md

