Today session distinguished failure types for the first time cleanly:
- Melting points 53% off: fitting failure
- Critical exponents 2x off: theoretical framing failure (Landau analogy doesn't hold)
- TEST-04a sign reversed: mechanism-class failure (the mechanism predicts the wrong sign)

The mechanism-class failure taxonomy is the new intellectual contribution of this session.
It tells the framework what can be rescued by retuning (magnitude misses) and what requires
mechanism replacement (sign reversals). This is discovery, not documentation.

The N_corr gap is equally important: without a Hamiltonian->N_corr protocol, the framework
